//Aggregation

Aggregation is also a "has-a" relationship, but the contained object can exist independently of the container.

Example:

class Teacher {
public:
    string name;
};

class School {
public:
    Teacher* teacher;

    School(Teacher* t) {
        teacher = t;
    }
};

Now:

Teacher t;
School s(&t);

Here:

School has a Teacher
But the Teacher can exist without the School
Teacher
   ↑
   |
School

If School is destroyed, Teacher t can still exist.

Composition vs Aggregation

Composition:

Car has an Engine → strong ownership

Aggregation:

School has a Teacher → weaker relationship; Teacher can exist independently

Simple definition:

Aggregation = a class has a relationship with another object, but that object can exist independently of the class.